1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,830
Drop a pinch of salt into

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:02,150
water,

3
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,050
and it seems to vanish.

4
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:04,190
But where does it go?

5
00:00:04,490 --> 00:00:05,400
Salt is a crystal:

6
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:06,780
sodium and chloride ions,

7
00:00:06,870 --> 00:00:08,200
locked together by opposite charges.

8
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,350
Water molecules are tiny magnets of

9
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:10,670
charge:

10
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:12,190
slightly negative at the oxygen,

11
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:13,870
slightly positive at the hydrogens.

12
00:00:14,170 --> 00:00:15,320
At the edges of the crystal,

13
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:16,120
they crowd in,

14
00:00:16,170 --> 00:00:17,300
oxygens toward sodium,

15
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:18,480
hydrogens toward chloride,

16
00:00:18,570 --> 00:00:18,960
and tug.

17
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:20,070
One by one,

18
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,190
the ions break free,

19
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:22,530
each wrapped in its own shell

20
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:22,890
of water.

21
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:24,140
That is dissolving:

22
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:24,900
not vanishing,

23
00:00:25,070 --> 00:00:26,080
just spreading out,

24
00:00:25,930 --> 00:00:27,040
one ion at a time.
